ng before it became a buzzword here  Russian government propagandists making  fake ukrainian facebook profiles and  using those to drum up local fears and  tensions and ukrainian human rights  monitors say that where this  disinformation warfare was strongest  actual violence has also been highest so  can Facebook really get away with  separating its online platform from the  offline effects it's enabling Unilever  just pulled their ad dollars until  Facebook and clean up their fake news  problem because they'd rather be part of  the responsible solution than be  responsible for the problem next six  point three trillion dollars this is  where we get to start building the  business case for why good business can  be good for business why we're gonna  have to start caring about things like  the human rights impact of our work six  point three trillion is the value of  assets under management at Blackrock the  world's largest asset manager and their  chairman Larry Fink just wrote a letter  to CEOs putting them on notice the  Blackrock is going to become a more  engaged investor one demanding that its  companies serve not only their  shareholders but also society Vanguard  CEO with their four point eight trillion  is planning to follow suit this is  really my kind of competition  all that means that like this isn't  going to be just about what like  watered-down CS are but about  integrating this into core business  functions so access to investment is one  real reason that a whole variety of  human costs now need to be built into  your business's bottom line I'll quickly  give you three more first reputation  it's hard to quantify but we all know  it's incredibly important a single  scandal that links to your brand to a  human rights abuse no matter how far  away it can be devastating for sales and  reputation and on the up side company is  with values oriented reputations tend to  suffer less of a stock hit when problems  do come up  second there's improved supply chains  applying a responsible sourcing lens  means that you can reduce costs by  building better supplier relationships  or avoiding disruptions third  Millennials like us care about choosing  to work for places that are doing good  as Millennials nearly half of us in this  room say our loyalty to our employer  would increase if we knew our CEO was  ahead of the pack on social issues all  this means that if you want to attract  high quality investment earn a resilient  reputation build responsive supply  chains and get the best talent you just  have to figure out how to be part of the  responsible solution not responsible for  the problem which brings me to my last  number one one person that could be you  and not just your CSR team but you as  you face your next business challenge  set standards for your company and its  values measure against them commit to  digging into hard problems instead of  walking away there's no easy playbook  for this but we now know we have to  figure it out it's asking who and where  are all the people whose lie  are affected by this business choice  from website to farm to factory to mine  and so the last number is one of hope  because real CSR doesn't have to be a  burden it can be the next business  opportunity  it starts with one responsible person  asking one responsible question getting  on the path toward being responsible not  for the problem but for the next  solution thank you  [Applause]  [Music]

